@startuml
title E02 - Reliable transport and duplicate handling
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
control "N05\nNode storage" as N05
control "N02\nNode radio" as N02
control "S01\nShared contracts" as S01
control "H01\nHub ingest" as H01
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
control "B03\nEvent ingestion" as B03
N05 -> N02: Expose oldest retained event
N02 -> S01: Encode node event v1 with stable event/session/sequence IDs
N02 -> H01: Send or retry with bounded jitter
H01 -> H02: Authorize and commit event key once
H02 --> N02: Return VOLATILE, DURABLE or policy-discard ACK
N02 -> N05: Retire only on DURABLE/policy-discard
H02 -> H08: Replay uncommitted cloud outbox item
H08 -> B03: Publish CloudEvent; transport ACK is insufficient
B03 -> B03: Unique (home,event) insert or return prior commit
B03 --> H08: Application-commit ACK
note over N02,B03: Duplicates may cross either link, but domain effects remain exactly once by stable key.
note over N05,B03: Outcome - Events survive loss/retry and duplicate delivery without being deleted before durable downstream commitment.
@enduml
